# Hand-port of the Zimbra nginx patch hunks that do not apply to nginx 1.30.7 (apply with -p1, after Zimbra's 23 patches).
# Covers: --with-mail-sasl option vars, upstream server 'version=' + NGX_HTTP_UPSTREAM_VERSION + connect hook,
# exact_version_check, ssl_session_reuse guard, mail handler (SASL includes, AUTH PLAIN/LOGIN abort + length checks),
# IMAP parser state rename (swi_*) + RFC3501 backslash rule, IMAP upstream response parser, and the
# 'return;' -> ZM_LOOKUP_SSL_EVENT_FAILED bug fix in ngx_zm_lookup.c, and upstream keepalive (implicit since 1.29.7)
# off by default + NGX_AGAIN passthrough in the keepalive peer init (zmauth route lookup is asynchronous). NOT ported on purpose: max_headers
# (native in 1.30) and the removal of ngx_ssl_ocsp_cleanup() in ngx_event_openssl.c.

